# Python bytecode.
#
# 294 .pyc files were committed by mistake in 505a0cf (2026-09-08) during the
# repository split. Because they are tracked AND regenerated on every test
# run, the working tree was permanently dirty, and `git pull --rebase` then
# refuses outright:
#
#     error: cannot pull with rebase: You have unstaged changes.
#
# That blocks the rebase-then-push cycle most sessions land with (AGENTS.md), for
# every chat working in this repository. They are also machine-specific
# (cpython-314) and rebuilt automatically, so they carry no information.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Test and packaging artefacts.
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Virtualenvs. A venv built by scripts/install.sh already ignores itself
# (.venv/.gitignore holds `*`); this covers one created any other way.
.venv/
venv/

# Rendered documentation. `docs/_build/` is what a local `sphinx-build`
# writes by default; `public/` is what the docs-build CI job writes and
# uploads as an artifact.
docs/_build/
/public/
